# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output.
#
# Pages sets Content-Type from a mime lookup, then applies this file, so a rule here
# overrides the lookup. Without these rules:
#   .cs -> no mime entry -> application/octet-stream -> the browser downloads the file
#          and some agent fetchers refuse a non-text content type.
#   .md -> text/markdown -> most browsers download it.
#
# text/plain, not text/markdown: browsers render text/plain inline and every agent
# fetcher accepts it. Nothing that reads these files needs the markdown media type.
#
# A rule compiles to ^...$ with * replaced by a capture group, so an extension suffix
# matches. Keep the rules disjoint: two rules that set the same header on one path are
# joined with a comma, not overridden.
#
# Do not add access-control-allow-origin. Pages already sends "*" on every asset.

/*.md
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/*.cs
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
